// SM3 (GB/T 32905-2016, as described in "The SM3 Cryptographic Hash Function", draft-sca-cfrg-sm3-02, Shen, Lee, Tse, Wong,
// Yang, CFRG / IETF, January 2018), written from the draft's Section 4-5 (IV, T_j, FF_j/GG_j, P_0/P_1, message expansion,
// compression function, padding). Checks the draft's two worked examples from GB/T 32905-2016, "abc" (1 block) and "abcd"
// repeated 16 times (2 blocks): per block the 68 words W and 64 words W' of the expanded message, the 8 registers after each
// of the 64 rounds, and the block's output chaining value. In all 591 published values: 396 expansion words, 192 round
// states (of 8 registers each), the chaining value V_1 of example 2, and the two final digests. The published values are
// data copied as numbers; no code from the draft's appendix was copied. Exit 0 only if all 591 match.
// Negative control: -DSM3_T2=0x7a879d8bU changes one bit of the constant T_j used for rounds 16..63.
#include "ounce_paper.h"

